{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>YHWH acquired me, the beginning</b> — this too is from the words of Wisdom." "<b>Acquired me</b> — from the root of: <i>Heaven's Acquirer</i> [i.e., Creator of heaven]." "<b>The beginning of His way</b> — that is, the beginning of His intention in creation, as in: <i>For He is the beginning of His way to El</i> [cf. Job 22(?)] [cf. Proverbs 8:22(?)] [cf. the phrase in Ibn Ezra's source]." "<b>From of old, from the beginning, His works of old</b> — קדם, like ראשית, and the meaning: priority to the world, priority of necessity not priority of time, for time is included among the created things, as it says: <i>YHWH founded the earth by Wisdom</i> [Proverbs 3:19]."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {2 "The comparison phrase כי הוא ראשית דרכי אל does not correspond to any standard biblical verse; translated hyper-literally as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:21:31.573048654Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}